<title>SWITZERLAND: Sulzer shares fall after suit news.</title>
<headline>Sulzer shares fall after suit news.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swiss engineering group Sulzer AG's was down about 12 Swiss francs from opening levels after news that the company expected a lower 1996 profit as a result of a patent suit in the U.S.</p>
<p>Sulzer's shares were trading at 700 francs at 0905 GMT, down from an opening of 712 francs and a 711 franc Wednesday finish.</p>
<p>Sulzer said earlier that a U.S. appeals court ruled that its Intermedics Inc unit must pay the $73 million damages awarded to Stryker Corp in connection with an earlier ruling in a patent suit. -- Zurich Editorial +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
